course: dictionary
lesson: 13946
title: Words about words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A lexicographer is a person who writes or edits dictionaries. Each word in a dictionary needs its meaning checked, and a lexicographer makes sure it is right. «The lexicographer read the new word three times before writing its meaning.»
explain: Look at the word itself for clues. Lexicographer ends in -er, like teacher and baker, and -er often means a person who does a job. The middle part sounds like lexicon, which is an old word for a list of words. So a lexicographer is a person who works with a list of words.
explain: Two famous lexicographers are Samuel Johnson and Noah Webster. «Samuel Johnson wrote a famous English dictionary in 1755.» «Noah Webster wrote an American dictionary in 1828.» Both did the same kind of work, but in different countries and at different times.
fact: A lexicographer is a person who writes or edits dictionaries.
fact: The -er at the end of lexicographer shows a person who does a job, like teacher or baker.
fact: Samuel Johnson wrote a famous English dictionary in 1755.
fact: Noah Webster wrote an American dictionary in 1828.
fact: A lexicographer studies how words are really used, then writes the meaning and an example sentence.
exercise: «The lexicographer spent ten years writing the new dictionary.» Who is the lexicographer? | A person who reads the news on television | *A person who writes dictionaries | A person who sells books in a shop | A person who drives a bus
exercise: The ending -er in lexicographer shows: | *a person who does something | a place where something happens | a colour | a question
exercise: Who wrote an American dictionary in 1828? | Isaac Newton | Samuel Johnson | *Noah Webster | Charles Dickens
test: Which word means a person who writes or edits dictionaries? | librarian | author | *lexicographer | teacher
test: «The lexicographer checked each meaning carefully.» Here checked means: | ate | lost | painted | *looked at again to make sure it is right
exam: «Samuel Johnson wrote a famous English dictionary in 1755.» What was Samuel Johnson? | *A lexicographer who wrote a famous English dictionary | A sailor who sailed to America | A king of England in 1755 | A painter who drew English gardens
